y high linearity of over 99.7  and this allows for more accurate and  precise measurements  of fluctuations and fluorescence and  this is going to be important whenever  we're relying on these to make  quantitative measurements  and another thing that we looked at  as well was to do with minimizing  vibration  within the camera and that is done in a  number of ways  and we also have water cooling as an  option so that again is another  way to eliminate issues with the  vibration  impacting sensitive measurements and  having any impact on trying to  localize a so sometimes only any mctd  camera  will do it's just not possible  for even the latest sc mos cameras to  operate down to  signal photon per pixel levels  and um the exxon ultra 888  will provide the largest possible area  and speeds from emccd  so whenever we don't need that ultimate  sensitivity the  back illuminated scmos cameras like the  sona series  are going to prove to be a much better  solution for super resolution or fcs  so we can make use of the smaller pixels  and  take benefits of the improved sampling  improve spatial information  and potentially get some better  localization accuracy as a result of  that  we can also get higher frame rates  higher speeds and better dynamic range  as well  and the sony models have been optimized  really to deliver and extract the best  from those latest sensors and get the  best accuracy and precision  possible from quantitative measurements  such as  as you as used within super resolution  and fcs  experiments so there's a wide range of  super resolution  techniques out there so experimental  requirements as well are also going to  vary quite a lot  so it's always recommended to contact  one of your local and or representatives  to discuss  whatever may be your specific  requirements  okay thank you so now we can move back  to  questions for the main part of this  webinar  thank you gentlemen for your informative  presentations  we will now start the live q a p